---
import originalResults from "../../../public/data/historical-comparison/results.json";
import { datasetJson, refreshedDataDirectory } from "../../data/dataset-input";
import { snapshot } from "../../data/results";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const results = datasetJson(
	"historical-comparison/results.json",
	originalResults,
);
const reproduceCommand = `uv run python scripts/reproduce_historical_comparison.py /path/to/downloaded/historical-comparison/inputs.json /tmp/historical-results.json --expected-case-count ${results.available_cases} --expected-unit-count ${results.available_units}`;
const names: Record<string, string> = {
	"google:gemini-3.7-flash": "Gemini 3.7 Flash",
	"openai:gpt-5.6-luna": "GPT-5.6 Luna",
};
---
<Layout title="Historical full-packet results | LegalForecastBench" description="Separate exploratory results reconstructed from two saved runs on the earlier 100-case corpus, with prediction failures and outcome coverage disclosed.">
  <section class="prose-lfb prose mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <a href="/data/run-notes/">← Run notes</a>
    <h1>Historical full-packet results</h1>
    <p>These two saved runs used the earlier 100-case corpus, before the corpus factory cutover. They are exploratory historical results: the earlier corpus had missing filed oppositions, and these results are separate from the current {snapshot.cohort.case_count}-case comparison and its rankings.</p>
    <p>Both configurations requested high reasoning with the older Inspect AI full-packet backend. Each case recorded one model request and no tool calls. These records do not establish execution with the current native document-tool agent. GPT-5.6 Luna requested the Flex service tier.</p>
    <p>The downloadable cohort contains {results.available_units} prediction units from {results.available_cases} cases. Frozen labels provide binary outcomes for {results.labelled_units} units; {results.null_outcome_units} have null outcomes and are excluded from scoring. Nullable outcomes remain in the reproduction download. {refreshedDataDirectory && "Withdrawn cases have been removed from this historical extract as well as the current comparison."}</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Accepted / attempted cases</th><th>Scored cases / units</th><th>Micro Brier</th><th>Equal-case Brier</th><th>All-execution estimated cost</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{results.conditions.map(row => <tr><td>{names[row.model_id]}</td><td>{row.accepted_cases} / {row.attempted_cases}</td><td>{row.scored_cases} / {row.scored_units}</td><td>{row.micro_brier.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{row.equal_case_brier.toFixed(6)}</td><td>${row.estimated_all_execution_cost_usd.toFixed(6)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>{results.conditions.map(row => `${names[row.model_id]}: ${row.failed_cases.length} rejected case outputs, ${row.dropped_labelled_units} labelled units dropped; ${row.scored_units} scored units across ${row.scored_cases} cases.`).join(" ")} These unequal denominators do not support a ranking or significance claim.</p>
    <p>Recorded token usage and estimated costs cover all attempted cases in this downloadable historical cohort, including rejected outputs. They are recorded estimates, not provider invoices or standard-rate repricing. Cache dimensions and billing evidence are unavailable here. The results download reports accepted-workload estimates and usage coverage separately.</p>
    <h2>Reproduce without model calls</h2>
    <p><a href="/data/historical-comparison/inputs.json" download>Download original unit probabilities, nullable outcomes, usage, and run identities</a> · <a href="/data/historical-comparison/results.json" download>Download reconstructed results and failed-case details</a></p>
    <p>From the repository checkout, run:</p>
    <pre><code>{reproduceCommand}</code></pre>
    <p>The script validates case and unit coverage, rejects malformed or defaulted inputs, and uses the benchmark’s shared scorer for micro and equal-case Brier. The sanitized extract contains no court documents, model rationales, or private operating records. Saved run IDs are {results.conditions.map(row => row.run_id).join(" and ")}.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
